    <string name="set_usb_note">On Android 14+ with a USB DAC attached, the app requests bit-perfect passthrough at 32-bit / 384 kHz (stepping down to 192/96/48 kHz if refused); otherwise it falls back to the system mixer.</string>
    <string name="set_ncm_auto_long">When scanning authorised folders, files are converted automatically: FLAC first; if FLAC is not possible it falls back to MP3 or publishes the original instead of failing. Output goes to your export folder (or app-private files/music/ncm if unset); originals are kept.</string>
    <string name="set_add_folder">Add music / ncm folder</string>
    <string name="set_export_at">%1$s (converted FLAC / MP3 are exported here and survive uninstalling the app)</string>
    <string name="set_no_tree_a">No folder authorised yet. NetEase ncm downloads live in /storage/emulated/0/download/netease/cloudmusic/Music, </string>
    <string name="set_no_tree_b">and the button above opens that folder directly; anything inside Android/data/com.netease.cloudmusic is protected by the system and unreadable by third-party apps.</string>
    <string name="set_no_tree_c">Note that the Download root itself cannot be authorised, only its subfolders.</string>
    <string name="set_scrape_note">Only fills gaps: songs that already have artwork or lyrics are skipped. Sources: iTunes and Deezer for covers, LRCLIB for lyrics; results are cached in the app folder and work offline afterwards.</string>
    <string name="set_netease_note">Prefers NetEase Music for covers and lyrics (undocumented API, no account needed; it may be rate-limited or break, in which case it falls back to iTunes / Deezer / LRCLIB).</string>
    <string name="set_restore_covers_sub">Removes scraped covers so embedded or system album art shows again (covers you set manually are kept)</string>
    <string name="set_clear_scraped_sub">Only removes automatically downloaded covers (manual ones are kept), then re-scrapes immediately with the fixed logic</string>
    <string name="set_tint_note">Tinted glass absorbs light: the deeper the colour and the lower the transmission, the darker it gets. Only the wheel ring is affected; dock, top bar and playback controls stay clear.</string>
